    {
      "id": "RPI-02",
      "chapter": "global",
      "anchor": "global-real-parabolic-gauge",
      "title": "The compact intersection and the Hilbert–Schmidt Jacobian",
      "statement": "With compact mass one, the one-place coefficient is 2^(−dim N/2) vol(K)/vol(M∩K), both volumes measured in the induced Hilbert–Schmidt metric. This coefficient is π for the isotropic line in U(1,1).",
      "hypotheses": "The same local flag and gauges. The compact intersection has one doubled unitary block of rank jᵢ per jump and single residual blocks of ranks p−Σjᵢ and q−Σjᵢ.",
